<description>&lt;p&gt;US has taken a fugitive businessman into custody in Venezuela on bribery charges, while Maduro and Flores face formal US charges for ordering torture, sparking protests. An aid worker describes earthquake damage in Venezuela as shocking, and Rubio calls on all opposition figures to join talks with the government. Starlink internet is now allowed to operate in Venezuela and Cuba’s grid collapse is worsening regional strain. Energy firms are recruiting former US officials to access Venezuelan oil, and charges against Maduro allege a PDVSA plane was used to transport goods. There were 2 battle-related deaths in 2007, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Washington Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXkFVX3lxTE9LSF9RZW5GTEdOektnanhEMFJpbHFuRXJ1T0tGVUczVFBYNl9wMTRBZXF5SE90Z1BZdzJxc3FBMzRKaHVleWFydWhLVGVQTGdJVUd3aUpXUEFlcllnbmc?oc=5&quot;&gt;BBC&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiugFBVV95cUxPa2JSWGlDMFBqUGt6TUdQajNMT3Q4dWNWNDdGVVJPbkFyZnZXWTNneDNpNnRIWVpNUy11S1Z1cVVJWDNIM1VIbDNnX1FmQVhZNGgzUGFkMUY3Ynh4OGEtV2o4Xzg3OWtfZ0xJWEJMZGRTbnBCSUpGWmtBM2VkT1ZiY0ZaYk9xaHdYbVlyejdfak1FRXBsMlZjRVkyZnBIZjVHbXVPMVcxbm43MU03QWwyRjRST25xZFRJdlE?oc=5&quot;&gt;France 24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;6abc Philadelphia&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilgFBVV95cUxObDlrX3JTZnBWMjNwZjg2TUZ2ZGtJano3QUh4dWVoYjlhV2VBZDE2Vk1oU0xLS2ZYbjFPT2ZxU21iWmZjZzA2RkVuZC1mekhzSnJLbXhEYTNmWXJ2TU9BZXE3SzA5OHl5eERjTFpydU5TUWNIV0FhbmlJeW4wak0zQnRRUGNmRTJDWWQwcHhGNUFfZGFQQ0E?oc=5&quot;&gt;APWin&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihwFBVV95cUxOWnBITDI1UFhqMjlMaVA5ZVY0bHpDTzJ4UlFXcWp6RWpHaHB6VnMtbTVQc0w4SzVsOEgxbEQ2N205VmJZVjVEcm1VM2pfX29hVWtzMHNQQ3ByV